<title>USA: ADR REPORT - Ericsson rises.</title>
<headline>ADR REPORT - Ericsson rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telephone equipment company Telefon AB L.M. Ericsson rose Monday to highlight trade in American Depositary Receipts (ADRs).</p>
<p>Traders reported relatively slow trade but the strengthening dollar was boosting companies that have heavy sales in the United States.</p>
<p>Ericsson was up 1-1/8 to 30-3/8 in heavy trade in a rebound from a loss Friday.  The shares fell to 29-9/16 from 32-1/2 on Friday after the company reported strong earnings for the first quarter.  </p>
<p>CS First Boston cut Ericsson to buy from hold, and NatWest Securities downgraded the stock to hold from accumulate.</p>
<p>Dutch chemical company Akzo Nobel NV was off 2-1/8 to 63-7/8. Anglo-Dutch foods and consumer group Unilever NV was up 2-1/8 to 193-7/8, helped in part by the stronger dollar.</p>
<p>Royal Dutch Petroleum Co was up 7/8 to 177-1/8 ahead of earnings results Thursday.</p>
<p>Among Latin American shares, Brazilian telephone company Telebras SA rose 5/8 to 111-3/4.  </p>
<p>Decliners led advancers 364 to 187 among 806 ADRs. The ADR group was off 0.59 percent and volume in early afternoon was 63 million shares.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
